WEBVTT

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:32.790
What about the guests?

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.870
No problem.  All the guests went home.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.910
All right, close the shutters!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.460
Alright!

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.630
Hey!  What's wrong?

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.640
Hartman Vezelheim, Vincent van Hossen, Arima Isshin!

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:13.840
Hartman Vezelheim, Vincent van Hossen, Arima Isshin!

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.330
Hartman Vezelheim, Vincent van Hossen, Arima Isshin!

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.120
We would like you to remain silent.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:22.370
Josephine?!

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.580
That's...

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.210
This is Fujikura.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:35.510
Ridiculous!  To think that the Hills could be infiltrated this easily...

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:38.090
Josephine!  Don't tell me, you...

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.210
Can't see the forest for the trees, can you?

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:44.140
You always told me to use the utmost discretion in all matters.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.520
Milord!

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:51.860
Yuu, eh?  It looks like we've been captured, but we're unharmed.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.570
I leave Teppei to you.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.280
This guy!  He has established communication!

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.820
Then silence him!

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.450
I get it, I get it.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:06.880
I'm an old man.  I ask you to please restrain yourselves.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:09.970
I told you, didn't I?

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:15.470
By possessing money and power, you are always one step away from danger.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.300
This is Fujikura, acting under the direct supervision of Arima Teppei, heir apparent to the Arima Foundation.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.390
Give me a status report.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:28.940
No irregularities exist inside and outside of the country, except at Arima Hills.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.150
What about the situation at Arima Hills?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.820
Querying...the system is currently down, therefore it is impossible to confirm.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.030
Give me the status of the Arima SP.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.660
Mito, Saitama, Yokosuka, Hachoiji, all zones secured.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.370
Is this somehow related to Charl?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.430
Be quiet.  We have no intention of harming you.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.720
Sit up slowly.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.200
S-She's cute!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.970
Just like a doll!

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.750
We are merely here to accomplish our objective.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.070
If you don't resist, nothing bad will happen.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.590
Woah, they're huge!

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.200
They look really soft!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.060
You're annoying!  Shut up for a minute!

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:28.980
Y-Yes!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.710
Do we have a deal?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.470
All right, tie her up.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.230
Huh?  How?

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.060
Doing that is kind of...

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.570
<i>Normally!</i>  Do it normally!

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.420
Phew, "normally".  I was shocked.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.260
She's so cute, I thought that...

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.390
You morons!  We're on a mission!

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.600
Thank goodness.  You're all good people.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.210
Nah...

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.230
How the hell did I end up in the same team as these idiots?

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.190
You guys caused this blackout, right?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.200
Why would you do something like that?

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:06.130
There are many people who don't think highly of the Arima Foundation.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.760
That's how it is.  As a natural result, they collaborate with each other.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.470
Ouch!

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.180
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.270
Were you also the ones who called me here?

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.090
I cannot say anything about that.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.970
We are doing this job for our comrades.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.220
We have no intention of harming you unless you get in our way.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:29.100
However, if anyone interferes, we will have to stop them by any means.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.160
It's almost time.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.270
All right.  Show me the monitor.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.490
The media loves covering things like this.  It's an easy operation.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.280
A large-scale blackout has occurred in Roppongi.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.410
The cause is still unknown at this time.  There is no estimate of when power will be restored.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:55.030
What's the meaning of this?  They are covering it as if it were a mere power failure.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.000
That's odd.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.510
Thanks, Grandfather.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.470
You're a lifesaver.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.680
We've finished the preparations!

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.570
Thanks!

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.810
Well then, shall we give it another go?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.310
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.430
Someone knew about our plan to leak information.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.740
Our information was intercepted!

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.990
Houjouin, eh?

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.190
What an unexpected bonus.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.070
What's this?

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:23.990
What's wrong?

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.910
Someone is accessing the Hills' information network from outside!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.330
To think that we had a room like this...

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.300
...and Yuu, what's with that typing speed?

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.980
This is only natural for a maid.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.620
I see.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:47.340
Ah, it seems they've noticed.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:48.590
What do you mean?

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:52.850
They've noticed that I'm accessing the Hills' information network.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.180
A counterattack is coming.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.100
Counterattack?

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.000
It means that we're under attack.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.900
What'll happen?

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:05.950
If they're able to break through, the control of all of Arima Hills' systems will fall into enemy hands.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.280
They will be able to trace it back here, as well.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:13.820
Of course, I won't let them break through...that easily!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.300
We've regained control of the surveillance cameras.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.890
Ah, Milord!  Van Hossen-sama, as well!

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.620
Yuu-san, zoom in this camera's view!

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.300
Charl!

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.610
Phew, that was close.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:49.530
Did you regain control?

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:50.410
Yeah.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.700
Whoever it was, they were really skilled.  I had to get serious.

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:01.830
I'm sorry!  It appears they've sent us a DNA computer virus.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.610
Sorry, I don't really understand what you're saying.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.450
This type of virus...

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:07.970
Ah, explain it in twenty-five characters!

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:09.180
Note: japanese expression for "spell it out for me".

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.180
Ah, yes.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:09.300
This type of virus needs a set amount of time to act.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:09.420
This type of virus needs a set amount of time to act.

