00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:12.970
This type of virus needs a set amount of time to act.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.310
<i>Takes time?</i>  How long?

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:17.480
Twenty...no, ten minutes!

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:21.690
I'm going to the Hills.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:23.980
That's too dangerous!

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.980
We don't know who the enemy is or what they want.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.390
But, if I make a move, we may be able to find out.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.530
I'm going to the Hills.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.030
Teppei-sama!

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:40.150
The Arima group employees, Grandpa, Silvie's father, and Charl are all there.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:41.290
I will definitely save them.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.960
Understood.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:51.050
I will notify the Arima SP unit and ensure the safety of everyone there.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:52.800
I'm counting on you.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.270
To think that Teppei-sama will be riding this...

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:03.480
How can I express the gratitude of the entire staff?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.690
Do whatever you want...

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:09.940
Wait.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.820
I heard about what's going on from Fujikura-dono.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:14.940
It reeks of trouble.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:19.330
I'll come along even if you tell me not to.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.880
Do you guys have a spare helmet?

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.800
Silvie, hurry!

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.090
I know!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.780
They've left!  Chase them!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.350
This bike won't fall, right?

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.020
Yeah!

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:54.870
Damn!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.240
Teppei-sama?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.200
Yuu-san?

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.750
The research team members advise you to press the blue button.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.410
The blue button?

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.540
This one?

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.130
W-What the hell was that?  Damn them!

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:16.780
Teppei-dono!

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.010
Uh...also this one?

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.480
As if I'd fall for the same trick!

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:35.110
Arima's technology is amazing...

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.740
I'm glad we got rid of the legs before entering the city.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.490
Why are you trying to take over the Arima group?

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.480
All right, I'll answer that.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:58.610
However, I wonder if my words will reach you?

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.240
What do you mean?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.730
I was born in the slums.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:07.790
You could see Arima Hills pretty well from my home.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.920
From my house, it seemed like this building was heaven.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.860
Compared to that, my life was hell itself.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:21.370
Can you imagine my feelings, gazing at Heaven from Hell every day?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.140
From the moment you are born until the day you die, you are in Heaven.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.930
We will turn that Heaven into Hell.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.940
It's actually an unexpectedly interesting job.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.940
What're they doing?

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:36.490
Perverted things?

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.860
Ah, you shouldn't think about those things!

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:40.780
Sorry.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.620
I see. This path sure looks well lit.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.450
Yes.  It's because the main gate is being watched.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:51.580
What will we do?

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:53.000
We have no choice but to go.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.920
That's not one of your bad points.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:03.180
I see.  As if we really need to sneak in.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.560
Damn it, drinking in someone else's home?

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.090
Shall we bill them?

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.090
Yeah.  Make it two-fold.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:13.060
Teppei-sama,

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:16.560
we've neutralized the virus in the Arima Hills network,

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:20.320
regained control of the monitors, electricity, and the front gate.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:23.610
Understood.  Tell me everyone's location.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:28.880
Yes.  Milord, van Hossen-sama, and Vezelheim-sama are still in the conference room.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:32.830
Charlotte-sama is in the suite on the thirty-sixth floor.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:33.960
Thank you.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:34.540
Let's go!

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:35.500
Yeah.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.170
Teppei-sama, the enemy has begun to move.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:57.470
I am unable to locate an alternative route from your position.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:58.940
Shit!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:12:59.580
Wait!

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.850
If you go out recklessly, it's over!

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.360
There's no helping it.  Let's retreat for now.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:22.760
Arima Teppei-sama, I am Katayama of the Arima SP unit.  I apologize for being late.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.630
These people...

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:26.560
Thank you.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:28.830
Sorry, but I'm going to need everyone's help!

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:35.370
What's this?

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:42.650
You understand, right?  Don't hit the building!

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:48.000
To all attendants of the Arima Hills!

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.240
We're...

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.980
...going to debut here...

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:56.000
...on a big truck!

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.170
What is happening?

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:07.050
I heard all the details from Yuu.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:10.800
We're going to save that hapless princess.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.310
Houjouin!

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:18.510
This is...?  What's happening?

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.690
This deviates quite a bit from your original plan, Miss Josephine.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.860
No, wait.  There's one more thing.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:29.030
Ah, now you're in a bad mood?

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:32.090
Be quiet and obey your orders.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.500
Vincent-san, Isshin-san!  Now's the time!

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:43.040
Don't!  Hartman!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.340
Hurry!

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:52.930
It's true that I don't know what kind of life you lived.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.310
I can't even imagine it.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:58.890
Still, not all of it is our fault.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.440
It's not your fault, either.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:06.290
Why can't both sides understand each other?

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:10.650
Why do we have to be enemies?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:21.580
<i>Understand</i> each other?  You just told me that you can't even imagine our lifestyle!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:26.150
What is there to understand?  Why do you cling to such an illusion?

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:32.130
That's not it!  If you had reached out, I would have at least responded!

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.380
What would have happened if we had reached out?

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:40.810
It would have made our hellish situation even more pitiful.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:45.260
In the end, what you're saying is pure nonsense!

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:50.820
I'm glad I acted first.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:52.570
I don't know who the enemy is,

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.320
but this should mess up their plans.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.810
Yes.  The media may convey the happenings at Arima Hills,

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:04.290
but all that the people will see are those women down there.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.840
Don't call them <i>those women</i>!

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:10.800
They're the first idol group I've produced,

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.970
so make sure to buy the CD when it's released, okay?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.140
We've regained control of the security gates!

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:24.940
Security shutters closing.  We are locking up the enemy and allowing the SP units to enter.

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:31.410
The monitors indicate no abnormalities on the route from the roof to the suite room,

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.780
so please use the VIP elevator to get in.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:37.770
After that, you should be able to make contact from the shopping mall.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:38.660
Understood.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:39.950
Please open the hatch.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.580
It's too early!

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:45.300
I got shot at earlier, I'm still pretty wired.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.750
Jeez.  Open it up.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:04.940
Don't tell me she really did them in?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.520
She just knocked them out.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:09.730
Hey, what happened?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.780
Jack, what happened?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.110
Our helicopter has landed safely.  Jack-san is sleeping here.

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.360
You...!

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.280
I'm coming for you, just you wait!

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:20.740
Shit!

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:24.160
Trying to interfere with my plan?

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:28.290
Hey, now.  That's not very ladylike.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:32.800
Hartman was an apprentice of mine.  I'll have you take responsibility.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.000
Oh, excuse me.

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:38.550
Let him sleep in the next room!

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:39.170
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:43.430
It's about time to tell us your reason for coming here.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:46.750
Very well.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.910
We are the Pruss!

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:51.730
Pruss?

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:52.900
Indeed.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.690
Our goal is to embarrass the lot of you...

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:57.070
Embarrass?

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:57.950
That's right.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:03.120
Impressive, mobilizing this much manpower for such a thing.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:06.870
Even so, this is our tribute of sorts.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.670
Withdraw!

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.370
Withdraw!

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.750
Ah, it's over.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.760
Sheesh, just when things were getting interesting.

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:18.760
We're going home.

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.960
We've hidden a bomb in the Hills.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:26.730
We're pulling out.  Just a little longer, and...

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:28.060
..all right.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.050
This is odd.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:32.780
I thought so too.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:36.490
All the men disappeared in an instant.

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:38.360
What happened?

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.530
I don't know.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:41.100
In any case, we have to go.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.320
Yeah.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:47.000
Business floor, Hotel floor...we're regaining control, one right after the other.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:48.630
All the staff are safe.

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:53.670
Father!

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.820
Thank you, Silvie.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.400
I'm sorry for making you do this.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.260
Ah, what an awkward situation...

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:04.000
Where is Hartman?

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:15.440
Silvie!  I'm leaving them to you.  I'm going to save Charl!

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.070
Got it.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:18.570
Charl... Charl!

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:19.440
Charl...  Charl!

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.210
What would have happened if we had reached out?

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:40.360
It would have made our hellish situation even more pitiful.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:45.310
In the end, what you're saying is pure nonsense!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:46.880
That's not...

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:49.710
That's...

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:52.940
Charl!

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:56.000
Charl!

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:03.980
<i>Teppei!</i>

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:08.330
<i>Charl!</i>

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.440
Teppei!

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:23.890
Teppei!

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:29.910
Charlotte.

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:36.610
Teppei...I was so scared.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:42.110
It's alright now.  Everything is going to be fine.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.390
I see.  Allow me to express my gratitude.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.080
Thank you, Houjouin.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:54.610
Please contact me if you need help with your company.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.790
No thanks are needed.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.170
I just wanted to help Arima.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.590
By "Arima", I didn't mean the Arima Group.

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.080
I meant Arima Teppei!

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:11.180
W-Why are you laughing?

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:12.600
Well, I wonder?

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:14.850
Spit it out!

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:18.940
Teppei.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.650
That guy said something.

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:22.700
That guy?

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:25.570
He said that they set up a bomb in Arima Hills!

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.020
This kind of electrical interference...

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:45.630
Don't tell me...with something that simple, they...

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:29.490
Question!  Does Silvie always carry that sword around?

00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:32.610
Of course.  This is an heirloom which I received from the Emperor!

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:37.370
When I'm sleeping, when I'm in the bath, when I'm exercising, when I'm eating, when I'm watching a movie...

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:37.620
Next time on Princess Lover!  Red and Blue!

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:38.960
Hey, I'm not done yet!

00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:39.370
See you next time!
